  "explanation": "The question asks which country Rangaswamy Srinivasan is a citizen of. Two distinct historical claims are supported by the original sources:\n\n1. **United States**: Document D1S9 explicitly states that Srinivasan’s family moved to the United States in 1965, and he pursued his education and career there. This supports the claim that he is a U.S. citizen.\n\n2. **Dominion of India**: Document D2S3 and other sections of document d2 clearly state that Srinivasan was born in India during the British Raj and automatically became a citizen of the Dominion of India after independence in 1947. This is further supported by his own statements and biographical records.\n\nThere is no direct claim that Srinivasan is a citizen of modern-day India (C2) or Yugoslavia (C3), and these are either incidental or unsupported by the original sources."
}
